---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "./_privacy/privacy.scss";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  pageTitle="Crona privacy"
  description="Read Crona's privacy policy for what stays local, what telemetry can collect, and how to control it."
>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="page-header flow measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1>Crona privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-date">Effective date: May 16, 2026</p>
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        Crona is a local-first application. Your work data stays on your device. Telemetry is optional and disabled by default.
        This page explains what information can be collected when telemetry is enabled and how to control it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="privacy-toc page-body" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
      <a href="#scope">Scope</a>
      <a href="#at-a-glance">Privacy at a glance</a>
      <a href="#local-data">What stays on your device</a>
      <a href="#telemetry">What may be sent if telemetry is enabled</a>
      <a href="#anonymous-id">Anonymous identifier</a>
      <a href="#network-activity">Network activity</a>
      <a href="#use">How Crona uses information</a>
      <a href="#sharing">How Crona shares information</a>
      <a href="#retention">Retention</a>
      <a href="#choices">Your choices</a>
      <a href="#children">Children's privacy</a>
      <a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="privacy-body measure flow">
      <section id="scope" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>This policy covers the Crona app and the crona.work website.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="at-a-glance" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>2. Privacy at a glance</h2>
        <ul class="privacy-list">
          <li>Your work data stays on your device.</li>
          <li>Telemetry is optional and off by default.</li>
          <li>No account is required.</li>
          <li>Usage telemetry and crash reporting can be enabled separately.</li>
          <li>Crona does not sell data or use advertising identifiers.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="local-data" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>3. What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>Crona does not send your work data as telemetry, including:</p>
        <ul class="privacy-list">
          <li>Issues</li>
          <li>Habits</li>
          <li>Sessions</li>
          <li>Check-ins</li>
          <li>Exports</li>
          <li>Calendar content</li>
          <li>Notes</li>
          <li>Support bundle contents</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="telemetry" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>4. What may be sent if telemetry is enabled</h2>
        <p>If you enable telemetry, Crona may send:</p>
        <ul class="privacy-list">
          <li>Startup and shutdown events</li>
          <li>Release channel details</li>
          <li>Handled errors</li>
          <li>Panic errors</li>
          <li>App name and version</li>
          <li>Environment mode</li>
          <li>Whether the build is beta</li>
          <li>Operating system and architecture</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="anonymous-id" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>5. Anonymous identifier</h2>
        <p>
          When telemetry is enabled, Crona generates a random anonymous identifier and stores it locally. This lets repeated
          crashes and startup events be associated with the same installation without collecting your name, email address, or
          work data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="network-activity" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>6. Network activity</h2>
        <p>Crona does not require an internet connection for normal use.</p>
        <p>The app may contact external services only for limited cases:</p>
        <ul class="privacy-list">
          <li>GitHub or package sources for release/update information</li>
          <li>Telemetry services if you have enabled telemetry</li>
          <li>Support or diagnostic workflows you explicitly start</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No work data is sent during release checks or normal local use.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="use" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>7. How Crona uses information</h2>
        <p>
          Crona uses telemetry to understand crashes, startup behavior, release channel usage, and other stability signals.
          Error reports are sanitized before they are sent so they can help with debugging without including your work content
          or file paths.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>8. How Crona shares information</h2>
        <p>
          When telemetry is enabled, Crona sends analytics and error data to its telemetry provider for processing. It does
          not use this information for advertising and does not sell telemetry data to third parties.
        </p>
        <p>
          Official Crona releases include telemetry support, but no telemetry is sent until you provide consent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>9. Retention</h2>
        <p>Your work data stays local until you remove it from your device.</p>
        <p>
          Telemetry data is retained according to the telemetry provider's retention settings and is used only for
          troubleshooting, stability monitoring, and release diagnostics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="choices" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>10. Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          Usage telemetry and error reporting are both off until onboarding is complete and you enable them in the app. You
          can turn one on without the other if you want crash reporting without broader usage tracking.
        </p>
        <p>Open the in-app <strong>Privacy &amp; Diagnostics</strong> pane to review or change the setting at any time.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="children" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>11. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Crona is not directed to children under 13, and Crona does not knowingly collect personal information from children
          under 13.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If Crona changes its telemetry or privacy practices, this page will be updated so the current behavior stays documented here.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="privacy-section">
        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>For general support questions, use the <a href="/support/">support page</a>.</p>
        <p>
          For privacy concerns, use <a href="mailto:privacy@crona.work">privacy@crona.work</a> or a private security/privacy
          channel if one is available.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p>
        <a class="button" href="/support/">Open support</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
